<title>SOUTH KOREA: Dae Han to give up telecom business.</title>
<headline>Dae Han to give up telecom business.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Dae Han Pulp Co Ltd has decided to drop its plans to enter the wireless data communications business, the Korea Stock Exchange said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Dae Han had decided to give up its ambition in consideration of the uncertainty of business prospects and getting necessary approvals, the exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>The shares fell to their lower limit of 59,300 won, down 3,700, in afternoon trading.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
